From: H. James Zhao <hjz@squareup.com>
Subject: [PATCH] core: rpmb: translate init failures to STORAGE_NOT_AVAILABLE

The libutee persistent-object wrappers (TEE_OpenPersistentObject,
TEE_StartPersistentObjectEnumerator, TEE_CreatePersistentObject, ...)
call TEE_Panic() on any return code outside a narrow allow-list. When
RPMB is unusable because its auth key has not been provisioned on the
eMMC -- most commonly when CFG_RPMB_WRITE_KEY=n on an unprovisioned
device, in which case tee_rpmb_write_and_verify_key() returns
TEE_ERROR_BAD_STATE -- the raw error propagates through the RPMB FS
layer back to the TA and panics it inside libutee.

Translate non-allow-listed failures from tee_rpmb_init() to
TEE_ERROR_STORAGE_NOT_AVAILABLE, which is in the libutee allow-list.
Codes that libutee already tolerates (ITEM_NOT_FOUND, ACCESS_CONFLICT,
OUT_OF_MEMORY, CORRUPT_OBJECT, STORAGE_NOT_AVAILABLE) are preserved
unchanged so TAs still see accurate diagnostics for those conditions.

---
 core/tee/tee_rpmb_fs.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/tee/tee_rpmb_fs.c b/core/tee/tee_rpmb_fs.c
--- a/core/tee/tee_rpmb_fs.c
+++ b/core/tee/tee_rpmb_fs.c
@@ -1179,6 +1179,31 @@ static TEE_Result tee_rpmb_init(uint16_t dev_id)
 	}

 func_exit:
+	/*
+	 * The libutee persistent-object wrappers panic on any return code
+	 * outside a small allow-list (SUCCESS, ITEM_NOT_FOUND,
+	 * ACCESS_CONFLICT, OUT_OF_MEMORY, CORRUPT_OBJECT,
+	 * STORAGE_NOT_AVAILABLE). When RPMB is unusable -- most commonly
+	 * because the auth key has not been provisioned on the eMMC
+	 * (e.g. CFG_RPMB_WRITE_KEY=n on an unprovisioned device, yielding
+	 * TEE_ERROR_BAD_STATE here), propagating the raw error panics the
+	 * calling TA inside libutee. Translate non-allow-listed failures
+	 * to TEE_ERROR_STORAGE_NOT_AVAILABLE so TAs can handle the
+	 * condition gracefully, while preserving the codes libutee already
+	 * tolerates for accurate diagnostics.
+	 */
+	switch (res) {
+	case TEE_SUCCESS:
+	case TEE_ERROR_ITEM_NOT_FOUND:
+	case TEE_ERROR_ACCESS_CONFLICT:
+	case TEE_ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY:
+	case TEE_ERROR_CORRUPT_OBJECT:
+	case TEE_ERROR_STORAGE_NOT_AVAILABLE:
+		break;
+	default:
+		res = TEE_ERROR_STORAGE_NOT_AVAILABLE;
+		break;
+	}
 	return res;
 }

